pace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">symbolic,&nbsp;field,&nbsp;stochastic,&nbsp;recursive</span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3956" data-end="4122">where ⊕ denotes structured merge (homotopy colimit), reflecting that multiple computational modes combine multiplicatively rather than being reducible to scale alone.</p>
<hr data-start="4124" data-end="4127">
<h2 data-start="4129" data-end="4145">8. Conclusion</h2>
<p data-start="4146" data-end="4505">Joyce reframes Sutton’s “bitter lesson” as potentially an <em data-start="4204" data-end="4220">interim lesson</em>. Compute matters, but design principles might prove decisive once scale saturates. From RSVP’s perspective, this is not merely speculative: it provides a formal justification for hybrid architectures where <strong data-start="4427" data-end="4504">structured entropy-respecting computation outperforms brute scaling alone</strong>.</p>
