<p data-start="6447" data-end="6607">Here ⊕ denotes structured merge (homotopy colimit), implying that multiple encodings scale together, yielding richer and more resilient forms of intelligence.</p>
<hr data-start="6609" data-end="6612">
<h2 data-start="6614" data-end="6629">Conclusion</h2>
<p data-start="6630" data-end="7168">The history of film and computing demonstrates how seemingly small encoding choices can ratchet into global monopolies, foreclosing alternatives that might have flourished under different conditions. Sutton’s “bitter lesson” may thus be misread as a deterministic law of compute, when it is better seen as a story about how scaling amplifies contingent encodings. RSVP reimagines intelligence precisely by refusing ASCII- and token-centric ratchets, proposing instead a pluralistic, field-based path that keeps the roads not taken open.</p>
