D. Impact of the effective fluid on the growth of
perturbations
Eqs. (1)-(4) effectively describe an interacting DM-DE
model with ρDE = Λ+ρc+ρv. Since ρc and ρv are purely
phenomenological descriptions of dust interactions, they
have no physical meaning at a fluid-element level. We
therefore assume that, just like Λ, they do not cluster.4
Including the interaction term, the perturbation equa-
tions for the dust fluid in the Newtonian gauge and the
