<hr data-start="287" data-end="290">
<h1 data-start="292" data-end="337">Master Outline and Extension Instructions</h1>
<p data-start="339" data-end="519">This outline assumes your current essay draft is ~20 sections plus appendices. The goal is to <strong data-start="433" data-end="467">extend each into chapter-scale</strong> with expanded math, philosophy, and case studies.</p>
<hr data-start="521" data-end="524">
<h2 data-start="526" data-end="573">Part I — Foundations of Natural Philosophy</h2>
<h3 data-start="575" data-end="627">1. Introduction: Bitter Lessons, Sweet Lessons</h3>
<ul data-start="628" data-end="1073">
<li data-start="628" data-end="760">
<p data-start="630" data-end="760"><strong data-start="630" data-end="643">Extend by</strong>: tracing the Sutton “bitter lesson” debate, showing how scaling vs. design parallels in cosmology (ΛCDM vs. RSVP).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="761" data-end="960">
<p data-start="763" data-end="784"><strong data-start="763" data-end="781">Math insertion</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="787" data-end="960">
<li data-start="787" data-end="869">
